The reassignment and solution-row fixes are being completed together on the existing `paudley/454-rdflib-shim-algebra-level-reassignment` branch. No additional branch is needed.

The typed contextual route is integrated with current main. Native rows now have checked length, signed positional indexing and a lazy owning iterator; compatibility rows retain tuple iteration and their duplicate-label/asdict behavior. A fresh production wheel passed all28 irreducible boundary tests, including13 row-protocol cases, with no failures/skips/xfails and byte-exact verification of all27 installed package entries. Later projection-only Rust corrections passed71 existing Project, prepared, contextual and governor tests plus strict evaluator lint/format checks. Independent source and combined implementation reviews support the complete row contract; core semantics remain tested in Rust.

Native performance acceptance is still incomplete. Fresh emitted code confirms that repeated source-row decoding and an extra Lift transfer were removed. The complete projection audit finds remaining per-row outer-vector capacity/length bookkeeping versus the baseline bulk-write loop; that owning Rust cost is being repaired before acceptance. Successful compilation and identical untimed output samples do not override the emitted-body finding.

This is implemented, locally qualified work in progress, not published or merged completion. Final native-cost acceptance, normal signed hooks/commit/push, mandatory hosted qualification, PR review and governed integration/cleanup remain required. The combined PR will close both issues only after those gates pass. Preserved sibling work remains untouched until the qualified replacement lands.
